WEBVTT

1
00:00:04.400 --> 00:00:08.951
A cable is cut. The router
dies. The network has failed.

2
00:00:09.171 --> 00:00:12.979
What stops working? And where
does encryption keep data safe?

3
00:00:13.479 --> 00:00:17.752
A network failure is any break in
the connection between devices.

4
00:00:17.972 --> 00:00:22.105
A router with no power. A cut
cable. A server switched off.

5
00:00:22.325 --> 00:00:26.690
Or the wi-fi password is changed.
Any of these breaks the link.

6
00:00:26.910 --> 00:00:30.486
Some children think a failure
means the computers are broken.

7
00:00:30.706 --> 00:00:35.443
They are not. The computers are fine.
They just cannot reach each other.

8
00:00:35.943 --> 00:00:40.169
Everything that needed another
device stops. Start at school.

9
00:00:40.389 --> 00:00:44.336
Nothing prints. Saved work on
the server cannot be opened.

10
00:00:44.556 --> 00:00:49.850
The register cannot be sent. Now the
shop: the till cannot ask the bank.

11
00:00:50.070 --> 00:00:54.204
So it is cash only. At home
videos stop and calls drop.

12
00:00:54.424 --> 00:00:58.789
The smart speaker goes quiet. All
of them needed another device.

13
00:00:59.009 --> 00:01:04.628
Writing a story carries on. The calculator
carries on. They need nobody else.

14
00:01:05.128 --> 00:01:09.494
Encryption scrambles data so only
someone with the key can read it.

15
00:01:09.714 --> 00:01:13.615
Data on a network passes
through many devices on its way.

16
00:01:13.835 --> 00:01:17.225
Anyone who grabs it in the
middle sees only nonsense.

17
00:01:17.445 --> 00:01:21.253
Some children think encryption
hides that a message was sent.

18
00:01:21.473 --> 00:01:26.256
It hides what the message says. They
may see it went, and cannot read it.

19
00:01:26.756 --> 00:01:30.239
Your password is encrypted
before it leaves your device.

20
00:01:30.459 --> 00:01:34.174
A card number when you pay. A
private message to a friend.

21
00:01:34.394 --> 00:01:39.549
A medical record. The padlock in the
browser: that connection is encrypted.

22
00:01:39.769 --> 00:01:43.716
The password on your wi-fi encrypts
what travels through the air.

23
00:01:43.936 --> 00:01:47.512
Anything that would do harm if
a stranger read it is encrypted.

24
00:01:47.732 --> 00:01:51.169
A bus timetable is not,
because anyone may read it.

25
00:01:51.669 --> 00:01:55.338
Cybercrime is crime done
through computers and networks.

26
00:01:55.558 --> 00:01:59.737
Stealing data. Locking somebody's
files and demanding money.

27
00:01:59.957 --> 00:02:05.066
Pretending to be a bank to get a
password. Encryption is the main defence.

28
00:02:05.286 --> 00:02:10.162
A thief takes a laptop full of encrypted
records. They have taken a brick.

29
00:02:10.382 --> 00:02:15.676
The data is there and unreadable. That
is why hospitals and schools encrypt.

30
00:02:16.176 --> 00:02:19.659
A network failure breaks
the links, not the devices.

31
00:02:19.879 --> 00:02:23.780
The server is out of reach, so
saved work cannot be opened.

32
00:02:24.000 --> 00:02:27.947
Encryption scrambles data, and
only the key unscrambles it.

33
00:02:28.167 --> 00:02:33.136
Look for the padlock. Encryption is
the main defence against cybercrime.
